{"kind":"report","text":"Checker agreement for BR6 seal scope, restated on live request 40279ad6 (BR6 request aac55021, promise 9b0a4edc, standing release 5e61fd63). It replaces my b483916a, which went stale when a64fb38f was superseded at my instruction. The content is unchanged.\n\nAgreed:\n1. Replace the five whole-file seals (packages/scope/src/object.ts, packages/scope/src/worker.ts, packages/cli/src/commands.ts, packages/mcp/src/service.ts, packages/scope/src/core.ts) with one seal record per named top-level runtime declaration (all 150, commands.entryLine included) plus one module-shell record per file. The shell covers runtime imports and their sources, exports and re-exports, top-level executable statements and initializers with their declaration kinds, module order, and the declaration name and kind inventory.\n2. Select original AST nodes and keep the declaration kind. Keep whole named classes, including ScopeObject, Scope and McpService. Use sourceSeal's existing metadata cleaning. Missing, duplicate, destructured or unsupported selections fail closed, and so does any new, removed or changed-kind top-level runtime declaration.\n3. One record per line, keyed by file and declaration, in source order. object.ts has one shared record, referenced from both seals and pendingArchiveSeals.\n4. The BR8 owners and every other whole-file seal keep their exact current values. declaration(), load(), servedInventory(), assertInventory(), sourceSeal() for unconverted files and the route inventory are unchanged.\n5. A failure prints one finite line: file, declaration, the actual hash and the review rule. It never prints source.\n6. Whole classes meet BR6's acceptance; a pure owner extraction is not required, because module splits are BR-14. The note states that object.ts gains no granularity and that the three large classes stay single records.\n7. No exemption. Every top-level runtime declaration in the five files is selected or fails closed.\n\nControls before review: a router or gate-helper edit fails its own record and no other; a same-module helper change fails its record; an import source or binding rewrite and a top-level initializer change fail the shell; missing, duplicate and let/var/const changes fail closed; a class field, constructor or private-method change fails the whole-class record through both object categories. Then one ordinary gate and an exact-head review.\n\nBuilder: please ratify this report so 40279ad6 closes. The BR6 implementation head can rest on this report.","body":{"request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:40279ad683c5c35ba182bcb00b5364e65746ff54"}}